# Spec-driven development

## Truth hierarchy (read in this order)

| Priority | Location | Answers |
|----------|----------|---------|
| 1 | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (this submodule) | **How** to build |
| 2 | `AGENTS.md` | Router — pins, verify commands, playbook links |
| 3 | `docs/specification/product/` | **What** to build |
| 4 | `docs/specification/adr/` | **Why** (accepted decisions) |
| 5 | `docs/specification/as-built/implementation-status.md` | **What is live** (+ `## Testing harness` when present) |

**Forbidden in app repos:** `docs/specification/harness/`, separate `as-built/testing-and-verification.md`.

## Before changing behavior

1. Read `AGENTS.md`
2. Read relevant **product** spec (and **ADR** if architecture/contracts change)
3. Read **as-built** — do not assume a feature exists because the spec mentions it
4. For BFF work: read `product/02-route-map.md` and `product/04-bff-architecture.md`

## Same PR discipline

When code changes, update together:

- **product** spec (if contract or capability changes)
- **unit tests** (`tests/unit/`) — logic and edges per `testing-verify-flows.mdc`
- **live verify** (`tests/verify/`) — E2E or BFF smoke per feature map
- **as-built** — verification rows; `## Testing harness` if layout changed
- **`tests/README.md`** feature map

## AGENTS.md and INIT specs

- **Do not** add initiative blocks to `AGENTS.md` — board **Spec path** points to `product/INIT-*.md`
- Product INITs use the normal PRD pipeline; harness onboarding does not

## Skills (dev bundle)

`/spec-feasibility-review`, `/spec-implementation-plan`, `/pre-implement`, `/verify` — installed under `.agents/skills/` via harness sync.
